#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059496 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64edd709-3f6c-59e1-ae1f-bca25eca0483" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reflection of a Sine Curve Over the Horizontal Axis"}] :question/id #uuid "e03cba93-339e-578e-aae8-55c98669c2ff" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-4646" :question/problem "The graph above represents a transformed sine curve. What is the equation of the graph?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/259/Source/Images/89614702470515495bff6e9a7d2ee710.png)" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/259/Source/Images/da96b4325b5cb99127a208386e5d33a5.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=\\sin x$.\n- Then, reflect it in the $x$-axis to give $y=-\\sin x$.\n- Finally, stretch it parallel to the $y$-axis by a stretch factor of $8$ to give $y=-8\\sin x$.\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=-8\\sin x$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059497 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "85090bdf-4f1b-5f79-a751-48521ad98895" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reflection of a Sine or Cosine Curve Over the Vertical Axis"}] :question/id #uuid "4f63d3b6-1c1e-5cc3-8fe8-6f580a298c90" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-4647" :question/problem "The graph above shows the function $y=2\\sin(kx)$. What is the value of $k$?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/259/Source/Images/643d638672fe9059c6151e7469aa87c1.png)" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/259/Source/Images/eb76dc56d2a6336bf24e289a588ed2db.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=\\sin x$.\n- Then, reflect it across the $y$-axis.\n- Finally, stretch it parallel to the $y$-axis by a stretch factor of $2$.\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of\n\n$$\ny=2\\sin(-x)\n$$\n\nHence, $k=-1$.\n\nNotice that, because the sine function is odd, the $y$-axis reflection has the same effect as the $x$-axis reflection, i.e.,\n\n$$\n2\\sin(-x) = -2\\sin x\n$$\n\nSo the graph could also be viewed as $y=-2\\sin x$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059498 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1fe335eb-dc4a-5ea0-83cf-ad929e19b908" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reflection and Shifting of a Sine or Cosine Curve"}] :question/id #uuid "cbf9d044-3541-51fb-8131-3911909d334b" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-4648" :question/problem "The graph above represents a transformed cosine curve. What is the equation of the graph?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/259/Source/Images/8aaec5b66acc1171f90f49727710df5e.png)" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/259/Source/Images/7f231c9d8d6e80fb1a38e120cf2a63bc.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=\\cos x$.\n- Then, reflect it in the $x$-axis to give $y=-\\cos x$.\n- Finally, translate it by $2$ units **up** to give $y=-\\cos x+2$.\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of\n\n$$\ny=-\\cos x+2\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059499 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f71a8f16-93d4-5e5a-9b8b-e29efc682430" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reflection of a Cosine Curve Over the Horizontal Axis"}] :question/id #uuid "3e380a56-e9aa-58d6-8584-2da67a66bd02" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-4650" :question/problem "The graph above represents a transformed cosine curve. What is the equation of the graph?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/259/Source/Images/2a0825f8193233d0c8cb3a5362970095.png)" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/259/Source/Images/3be3200eb0bc3d37ac7b7b8e68404259.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=\\cos x$.\n- Then, reflect it in the $x$-axis to give $y=-\\cos x$.\n- Finally, stretch it parallel to the $y$-axis by a stretch factor of $6$ to give $y=-6\\cos x$.\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=-6\\cos x$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060286 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64edd709-3f6c-59e1-ae1f-bca25eca0483" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reflection of a Sine Curve Over the Horizontal Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8a12e03-7bf6-5ac3-82b1-af9cc21b81b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = π\\sin (x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058700} {:answer/id #uuid "ec32cb0d-2bce-55b3-bd65-1bfc5d7e99dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\sin (x) - π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058701} {:answer/id #uuid "14041484-fa99-5fc9-83c4-2cf98603cf7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-\\sin (πx)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058702} {:answer/id #uuid "4cee018c-40d7-57c2-85b2-4b2d7288563f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-\\sin (x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058703} {:answer/id #uuid "77fd0efd-af17-558b-b93f-45dc3bd64218" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\sin (x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058704}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4cee018c-40d7-57c2-85b2-4b2d7288563f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-\\sin (x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058703} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb0968ac-abba-5392-a5fe-c38d817e6fb4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058699}] :question/id #uuid "6d5ac861-a6f5-5aad-8010-c1a0229f1d0d" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-6580" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/259/Source/Images/q-6580.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the graph shown above?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060289 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "85090bdf-4f1b-5f79-a751-4